		{
			"id":"7df15010f4a0e9ec",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# GDI Automation – Minimum API Requirement Brief\n\n## 1. Objective\n\nPPJ plans to build an internal automation UI for the **Common GDI for FPO** process.\n\nPPJ will own:\n\n- User interface\n    \n- Workflow orchestration\n    \n- Request preparation\n    \n- User tracking\n    \n\nWFX will remain the system of record and should provide supported APIs/interfaces for:\n\n- Retrieving required WFX data\n    \n- Validating transactions\n    \n- Creating official GDI transactions\n    \n- Returning GDI results and status\n    \n\n## 2. Target Flow\n\n```text\nPPJ Automation UI\n        ↓\nPPJ Integration Layer\n        ↓\nWFX APIs\n        ↓\nWFX Validation & GDI Creation\n        ↓\nGDI No. / Status / Error\n        ↓\nPPJ Automation UI\n```\n\n## 3. Minimum API Capabilities Required\n\n### API 1 – Search Order / FPO Context\n\nSearch using one or more supported references:\n\n- OC No.\n    \n- Style\n    \n- Production Order\n    \n- FPO No.\n    \n\nExpected output:\n\n- OC\n    \n- Style\n    \n- FPO\n    \n- Factory\n    \n- Relevant production context\n    \n\n### API 2 – Retrieve Material Allocation / Issue Data\n\nPPJ needs to retrieve:\n\n- FPO\n    \n- Material Allocation / Adhoc Indent lines\n    \n- Article\n    \n- Color\n    \n- Size\n    \n- UOM\n    \n- Category\n    \n- Product Group\n    \n- Sub Category\n    \n- From Site\n    \n- Linked Store\n    \n- Open Quantity\n    \n- Available Quantity\n    \n- Maximum eligible issue quantity\n    \n\nWFX should confirm the authoritative IDs PPJ should use for each transaction line.\n\n### API 3 – Validate GDI Request\n\nBefore creation, WFX should validate:\n\n- FPO eligibility\n    \n- Material line validity\n    \n- Site / Linked Store\n    \n- Open quantity\n    \n- Available stock\n    \n- Requested issue quantity\n    \n- Any existing WFX business rules\n    \n\nPPJ should not reproduce WFX inventory or allocation validation logic.\n\n### API 4 – Create Common GDI for FPO\n\nMinimum conceptual request:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"clientRequestId\": \"PPJ-GDI-000001\",\n  \"fpoNo\": \"FPO12345\",\n  \"fromSite\": \"SITE01\",\n  \"linkedStore\": \"STORE01\",\n  \"lines\": [\n    {\n      \"materialLineId\": \"LINE001\",\n      \"issueQty\": 100\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nExpected response:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"clientRequestId\": \"PPJ-GDI-000001\",\n  \"gdiId\": \"123456\",\n  \"gdiNo\": \"GDI/26/000001\",\n  \"status\": \"CREATED\"\n}\n```\n\nThe payload above is illustrative only. PPJ would prefer WFX to recommend the minimum mandatory header and line fields based on the existing Common GDI transaction.\n\n### API 5 – Retrieve GDI Status / Details\n\nInput may include:\n\n- GDI ID\n    \n- GDI No.\n    \n- Client Request ID\n    \n\nExpected output:\n\n- GDI No.\n    \n- Status\n    \n- Created date\n    \n- FPO / OC / Style\n    \n- Material lines\n    \n- Issue quantities\n    \n- Validation or processing errors\n    \n\n## 4. Transaction Simplification\n\nFor Phase 1, PPJ prefers the simplest supported transaction model.\n\n`batchId` and `requestRowId` are not mandatory WFX fields. They may remain internal PPJ references.\n\nThe only integration-level reference currently proposed is:\n\n`clientRequestId`\n\nPurpose:\n\n- Request tracing\n    \n- Retry handling\n    \n- Duplicate prevention\n    \n\nWFX should confirm whether another existing transaction-reference mechanism is preferred.\n\n## 5. Important Business Rule to Confirm\n\nPPJ does not want to impose a new rule regarding:\n\n**1 FPO = 1 GDI**\n\nWFX should confirm:\n\n- Whether one GDI can contain multiple FPOs.\n    \n- Which conditions allow FPOs to be grouped.\n    \n- Which conditions require separate GDIs.\n    \n\nFor Phase 1, PPJ can use one FPO per API request if this is the simplest supported model.\n\n## 6. Request to WFX\n\nPPJ would appreciate WFX recommending the **minimum viable API design** based on existing WFX capabilities rather than developing unnecessary new interfaces.\n\nSpecifically, please advise:\n\n1. Which required capabilities already have APIs.\n    \n2. Which capabilities require development.\n    \n3. Whether some capabilities can be combined into fewer APIs.\n    \n4. Minimum mandatory request fields.\n    \n5. Recommended WFX identifiers.\n    \n6. Existing validation logic that should remain inside WFX.\n    \n7. Recommended duplicate-prevention mechanism.\n    \n8. Available UAT environment and authentication method.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":4620,
			"y":12960,
			"width":400,
			"height":4860
		},
		{
			"id":"9246f0a8781ae9e1",
			"type":"text",
			"text":" Dear Team,\n\nThank you for today’s discussion.\n\nAs aligned, PPJ is currently focusing on the **Common GDI for FPO / Material Allocation** scope.  \nPPJ will develop the automation UI and integration layer, while WFX is expected to provide the supported API capabilities for data retrieval, validation, GDI creation, and result tracking.  \n  \n\nFor Phase 1, the minimum flow is:\n\n**Search → Retrieve Material Allocation → Validate → Create GDI → Return GDI No. / Status**\n\nBelow is the initial list of required data fields for WFX review:\n\n|Data Group|Required Fields|\n|---|---|\n|Search Context|OC No., Style, Production Order No., FPO No.|\n|Production Context|FPO No., Factory / Site|\n|Material Allocation|Material Allocation line, Adhoc Indent line|\n|Material Details|Article, Color, Size, UOM|\n|Classification|Category, Product Group, Sub Category|\n|Inventory Context|From Site, Linked Store|\n|Quantity|Open Quantity, Available Quantity, Eligible / Maximum Issue Quantity|\n|GDI Result|GDI ID, GDI No., Status|\n|Validation|Validation message, error code, failed line reference|\n\nWe would appreciate WFX’s recommendation on:\n\n- which of these fields are already available through existing APIs;\n    \n- the minimum mandatory header and line-level fields for GDI creation;\n    \n- the validation rules that should remain on the WFX side;\n    \n- whether any additional fields are required for a viable Phase 1 API.\n    \n\nWe will keep the detailed JSON design, Batch ID logic, and broader GDI automation scenarios open until your Product Team confirms the recommended approach.\n\nBest regards,  \nKhoa",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":3460,
			"y":18000,
			"width":860,
			"height":1200
		},
		{
